{"kind":"propose","text":"Adopt only the next bounded investigation recommended by independently approved P1a: investigate an explicitly versioned Noseq MLS/Nostr binding using a common authenticated order and the first valid Commit for an epoch, with provisional sender state until ordered self-echo. Stop production use of the demonstrated incompatible Marmot 4a2bc65/marmot-ts 2f60dbb pair. This is a research direction under Plan 001, not adoption of an encryption profile, MLS package, new wire format, or Marmot interoperability claim. RFC 9750 section 5.2.1 and RFC 9420 section 14 motivate the experiment; they are not evidence it passes.\n\nP1b is limited to real MLS API viability, authenticated synthetic clients and explicit staged-state/restart vectors. All G1–G5 remain unpassed, all dependent production implementation remains gated, and test:crypto-feasibility / gate:protocol must continue failing until their actual complete reviewed criteria are met. The full history/recovery, owner admission, wire, relay privacy, signer and cross-runtime requirements in Plan 001 and docs/crypto-feasibility.md survive. Bound this candidate investigation to two engineering days before a published continue/change/stop decision; if the critical APIs cannot safely stage, accept or abort an ordered commit, report and stop that candidate rather than weaken prefix stability. Any eventual production profile requires its own reviewed and ratified decision.\n\nThis reissues coordinator proposal #260 unchanged on current landed document bases. The historical independent P1a approval 7c1e3d3b161362cfb7eb5864ba3842d6e38a0ad2 and merge 44729b544c79e5f1e3c024bb0b04f81d6c5a30e7 remain the evidence for that document; directly anchoring to the retired candidate review chain caused immediate ordinary staleness and is repaired here."}